      "notes": [
        "Keep substantive commit and comparison diffs visible when whitespace-only changes in other files are hidden.",
        "Let macOS debug builds run Git's interactive-rebase helper without Qt development environment overrides.",
        "Retain History actions while the repository is busy and retry automatically; replace outdated pending search and hover updates with the latest input.",
        "Prefill bisect from a selected commit pair and swap good/bad revisions. Search and choose commits in the picker's own results list without changing History.",
        "Prevent a bridge panic when bisect commit search selects its first match, and keep branch dropdown buttons inside the field outline.",
        "Search branches in worktree and auto-stash selectors, pick commits for bisect and rebase, and complete branch name path segments when creating or renaming branches.",
        "Refresh repositories with missing, prunable linked worktrees without reporting malformed reference data. Keep those worktrees visible with their Git identities.",
        "Load commit diffs with large binary assets using binary summaries instead of encoded binary patches, preserving text diffs within the existing output limit.",
        "Ensure macOS bundles include the Qt runtime search path and reject packages missing it before release.",
        "Use one diff component and matching view options in Changes and commit history, including word wrap, side-by-side layout, whitespace, and context controls.",
        "Add icons to the clean working tree and empty staged-files states.",
        "Stop Git commands that produce no output for their idle budget, while allowing commands that keep reporting progress to run longer.",
        "Add a Worktrees sidebar plus button and a creation form with starting ref, optional new branch, and a native folder picker. Select a worktree to inspect its branch in History; double-click to open it in a repository tab."
      ]
